    'eerst gezien {t}' => 'first seen {t}',
    'servers: {list}' => 'servers: {list}',
    'Nog niets bekend van dit IP-adres.' => 'Nothing known about this IP address yet.',
    'Tijdlijn van dit IP-adres' => 'Timeline of this IP address',
    'Server geïsoleerd of opgeheven' => 'Server isolated or lifted',
    'ISOLEREN' => 'ISOLATE',
    'VERGRENDELEN' => 'LOCK',
    '📜 Logs van webdiensten' => '📜 Web service logs',
    '(agent 1.58.0)' => '(agent 1.58.0)',
    'De agent leest elke minuut de nieuwe regels en vat ze per IP samen; RzSense herkent aanvallen. Waar staan de logs? Leeg of <code>auto</code> = zelf zoeken (de container van SWAG, gangbare mappen; in Home Assistant via de Supervisor). Je eigen netwerk en de whitelist tellen nooit.' => 'Every minute the agent reads the new lines and summarises them per IP; RzSense recognises attacks. Where are the logs? Empty or <code>auto</code> = search automatically (the SWAG container, common folders; in Home Assistant via the Supervisor). Your own network and the whitelist never count.',
    'nginx access-log (reverse proxy)' => 'nginx access log (reverse proxy)',
    'Home Assistant: home-assistant.log' => 'Home Assistant: home-assistant.log',
    'Vaultwarden: logbestand of container' => 'Vaultwarden: log file or container',
    'Scenario\'s' => 'Scenarios',
    '(elk apart aan of uit)' => '(each on or off separately)',
    'Web: <b>bekend aanvalspad</b> met een foutcode (<code>/.env</code>, <code>/.git/</code>, <code>wp-login.php</code>, <code>phpmyadmin</code> …): meteen' => 'Web: <b>known attack path</b> with an error code (<code>/.env</code>, <code>/.git/</code>, <code>wp-login.php</code>, <code>phpmyadmin</code> …): immediately',
    'Web: <b>scanner</b> (sqlmap, nikto, nuclei, zgrab …): meteen' => 'Web: <b>scanner</b> (sqlmap, nikto, nuclei, zgrab …): immediately',
    'Web: <b>veel 404</b>, vanaf' => 'Web: <b>many 404s</b>, from',
    'Web: <b>veel 401/403</b> (wachtwoorden raden), vanaf' => 'Web: <b>many 401/403s</b> (guessing passwords), from',
    'Web: <b>zonder hostnaam</b> (444, scant je IP-adres), vanaf' => 'Web: <b>without host name</b> (444, scanning your IP address), from',
    '<b>Home Assistant</b>: mislukte logins vanaf' => '<b>Home Assistant</b>: failed logins from',
    '<b>Vaultwarden</b> vanaf' => '<b>Vaultwarden</b> from',
    '…binnen (minuten)' => '…within (minutes)',
    'In de modus blokkeren zo\'n IP ook <b>blokkeren</b> (op al je servers, via <i>Automatische blokkades op alle servers</i>)' => 'In block mode also <b>block</b> such an IP (on all your servers, via <i>Automatic blocks on all servers</i>)',
    'Deblokkeren kan altijd bij <i>Blokkades en whitelist</i>. SWAG in Docker: de agent blokkeert vóór Docker (prerouting), dus ook verkeer naar de container wordt tegengehouden.' => 'Unblocking is always possible under <i>Blocks and whitelist</i>. SWAG in Docker: the agent blocks before Docker (prerouting), so traffic to the container is stopped too.',
    'Home Assistant ziet bij mislukte logins alleen interne adressen. Staat het achter SWAG, zet dan in configuration.yaml onder http: use_x_forwarded_for: true en trusted_proxies (het IP van SWAG); anders is een aanvaller niet te herkennen.' => 'Home Assistant only sees internal addresses for failed logins. If it is behind SWAG, set in configuration.yaml under http: use_x_forwarded_for: true and trusted_proxies (the IP of SWAG); otherwise an attacker cannot be recognised.',
    '{src}: {n} mislukte logins vanaf {ip}' => '{src}: {n} failed logins from {ip}',
    '{n} mislukte logins in {m} minuten (grens {limit}).' => '{n} failed logins in {m} minutes (limit {limit}).',
